# Test fixtures are byte-exact inputs to the lossless lint oracle. Never let the
# platform mutate their bytes (line-ending conversion, etc.) — treat them as
# binary so every checkout, on every OS, gets identical content.
#
# Why: with core.autocrlf=input, 68 .usfm fixtures silently carried CRLF in a
# local working tree while the committed blobs were LF. The oracle baseline was
# blessed against those CRLF bytes, so it passed locally but FAILED on every
# clean checkout (CI, fresh clone, git worktree). Pinning -text makes the corpus
# reproducible so the oracle is a real gate again.
testData/** -text
